From 5284c0539f22b57d5d82a5ab5ede1460d5b043fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 02:22:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] feat: decode camera RAW with rawpy and treat RAW+JPEG as
 one shot

RAW files were accepted by the scanner but never decoded with rawpy; TIFF-based
containers opened through Pillow as a small embedded preview and were scored as if
it were the photo. They are now decoded with rawpy (orientation, size limit and
EXIF capture time handled, half-size optional), and a clear per-file error says
what to install when rawpy is missing.

A JPEG sitting beside a same-named RAW is that RAW's companion: it takes no part
in grouping, ranking or best-shot selection and inherits the RAW's decisions, so
both files always land in the same bucket instead of being 'culled' as a burst.

Report schema 4 (additive): paired_with.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AVrJmEBWfEeojxr7zjNXdQ
