Subject: [PATCH 2/5] feat: verified, journalled and undoable organize;
 sidecars; group folders

- copies are checked against the SHA-256 recorded at analysis before being renamed
  into place; a cross-device move deletes its source only after that check
- every run is journalled (JSON Lines, fsynced, written before acting) to
  <dest>/.culler/undo/; `culler undo` reverses it, dry run by default, and never
  deletes a copy it cannot prove it made or whose original is gone
- .xmp/.aae/.pp3/... sidecars and Live Photo videos travel with their photo and
  follow its (collision-)renamed name
- --group-folders puts each burst/duplicate group in its own folder; a RAW's JPEG
  companion follows the RAW
- warns when the destination is inside the scanned folder
- replaces the single overwritten .culler_manifest.json with per-run journals

