From 4718b9b55e27e7e3641b42437691f944e68f29e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 08:12:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] feat: skip re-hashing unchanged files; CI on macOS/3.13
 plus a real-decoders job

Re-scanning an unchanged library re-read every byte just to recompute SHA-256.
The cache now remembers path+size+mtime -> sha256 (rsync-style quick check), so
a second scan of a 100 GB library does no file reads beyond headers.

CI: add macOS and Python 3.13, and a job that installs the real optional
decoders (rawpy, pillow-heif) so API breakage there is caught.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AVrJmEBWfEeojxr7zjNXdQ
---
